{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And the sun rose for him.</b> It is human speech: when we reached a certain place, the dawn lit up for us — this is its plain sense. And another says: <b>ויזרח לו</b> — for his need, to heal his limp, as you might say, ״שֶׁמֶשׁ צְדָקָה וּמַרְפֵּא בִּכְנָפֶיהָ״ (Malachi 3). And those hours that had hurried to set on his account when he left Be'er-sheva — they hurried to rise on his account." "<b>And he limped.</b> He was limping when the sun rose."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "The citation מלאכי ג' corresponds to Malachi 3:20 in the Hebrew verse numbering (3:20 = chapter 3 in the Talmudic/rabbinic three-chapter division of the Twelve Prophets)."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:51.888069043Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}